{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"installing-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installing components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> ui","source":"kirana-style ui"}},{"type":"text","value":" copies components from a registry into your project, as\nshadcn/ui's CLI does: the files become yours. It installs one source for every\nframework, rewrites its imports to your aliases, adds the packages it needs, and\nrecords what it wrote so it can update it later without losing your edits."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The commands live in their own package:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npm install --save-dev @kirana-style/registry","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npm</span> install <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--save-dev</span> @kirana-style/registry","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"setting-a-project-up","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting a project up"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style ui init","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui init","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"init","source":"init"}},{"type":"text","value":" works on a new app or one you already have:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"it sets Kirana up where the project lacks it, as "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> init","source":"kirana-style init"}},{"type":"text","value":" does;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"it maps the "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"@<span class=\"th-token th-comment\">/*</span>","source":"@/*"}},{"type":"text","value":" alias in "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"tsconfig.json","source":"tsconfig.json"}},{"type":"text","value":" when the project has none, and tells\nVite to read it;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"it installs the registry's design system and wires it in: its configuration in\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"kirana.config.ts","source":"kirana.config.ts"}},{"type":"text","value":", its reset beside Kirana's stylesheet, its styles on\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">html</span>&gt;","source":"<html>"}},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To start from nothing, take one of Kirana's examples, as the release you run has\nit:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style ui init --template vite-react my-app","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui init <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--template</span> vite-react my-app","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start with a design by its preset code, which a design system's site gives you:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style ui init --preset k2bS6","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui init <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--preset</span> k2bS6","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Name the framework or the base when the project depends on more than one, or a\ncomponent has several:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style ui init --framework react --base aria","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui init <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--framework</span> react <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--base</span> aria","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"adding-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adding components"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style ui add button dialog","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui add button dialog","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each component comes with the components it needs, in order. Its files land under\nyour alias for their type, "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"@/components/ui","source":"@/components/ui"}},{"type":"text","value":" for components by default, and its\nicons are drawn with your icon library. The packages it needs are installed with\nyour package manager, and Kirana checks what was written before your next build."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"add","source":"add"}},{"type":"text","value":" never changes a file you already have unless you pass "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-variable\">--overwrite</span>","source":"--overwrite"}},{"type":"text","value":".\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--dry-run</span>","source":"--dry-run"}},{"type":"text","value":" shows what it would do."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-lockfile","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The lockfile"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"kirana-style.lock.json","source":"kirana-style.lock.json"}},{"type":"text","value":" records each installed component: the registry it came\nfrom, its version, the framework and base, and for each file two hashes. One is\nof the registry's content, the other of what was written. Commit it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The two hashes are how the later commands tell the registry's change from yours:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style ui outdated\nnpx kirana-style ui diff button","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui outdated\n<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui diff button","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"changing-the-design","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changing the design"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A design system says which axes it has (a style, a base colour, a radius …) and\nhow a preset code holds them. Give a code to "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"init","source":"init"}},{"type":"text","value":", or change it later:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style ui preset k2bS6","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui preset k2bS6","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"preset","source":"preset"}},{"type":"text","value":" writes the design to "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"ui.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">design</span>","source":"ui.design"}},{"type":"text","value":" and sets its attributes on "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">html</span>&gt;","source":"<html>"}},{"type":"text","value":",\nwhere your design system's styles are. Then it places every installed component\nagain: a registry that flattened its style modules for the new design gives you\nthat build, with only the new style's values in it. A file you changed stops it\nuntil you look, or pass "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-variable\">--overwrite</span>","source":"--overwrite"}},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"updating-and-removing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Updating and removing"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style ui update","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui update","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"update","source":"update"}},{"type":"text","value":" writes what the registry changed and keeps what you changed. Where both\nof you changed the same file, it stops before writing anything: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"ui diff","source":"ui diff"}},{"type":"text","value":" shows\nthe two sides, and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-variable\">--overwrite</span>","source":"--overwrite"}},{"type":"text","value":" takes the registry's. A registry that changes a\ncomponent's files without a new version is refused."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style ui remove dialog","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui remove dialog","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"remove","source":"remove"}},{"type":"text","value":" deletes the files you left as they were installed and keeps the ones you\nchanged. It refuses a component another installed one still needs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"your-registries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your registries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kirana UI's registry is known as "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"@kirana","source":"@kirana"}},{"type":"text","value":". Name others in "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"kirana.config.ts","source":"kirana.config.ts"}},{"type":"text","value":",\nunder "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/reference/config#ui","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"ui.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">registries</span>","source":"ui.registries"}}]},{"type":"text","value":", and install from them by\nnamespace:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style ui add @acme/card","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style ui add @acme/card","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/registries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Publishing a registry"}]},{"type":"text","value":" describes the format, for\nyour own."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installing-components","text":"Installing components","level":1},{"id":"setting-a-project-up","text":"Setting a project up","level":2},{"id":"adding-components","text":"Adding components","level":2},{"id":"the-lockfile","text":"The lockfile","level":2},{"id":"changing-the-design","text":"Changing the design","level":2},{"id":"updating-and-removing","text":"Updating and removing","level":2},{"id":"your-registries","text":"Your registries","level":2}]}
